
  <sn><md>### Basic Data Types in C

A **data type** tells the compiler **what kind of data** a variable can store.

C has several basic data types:

| Data Type | Stores                       | Example                    |
| --------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `char`    | A single character           | `'A'`                      |
| `int`     | Whole numbers                | `10`                       |
| `float`   | Decimal numbers              | `3.14`                     |
| `double`  | More precise decimal numbers | `3.14159265`               |
| `void`    | No value                     | Used mainly with functions |
</md></sn>
